«
@@ ============================================================
@@ PolarFit — fit a parabolic drag polar to measured points.
@@
@@ Input:  a list of points { CL CD }, lift and drag coefficients,
@@         at least two with different lift coefficients.
@@ Output: CD0 and Kind of the polar CD = CD0 + Kind·CL², fitted by
@@         least squares on CL², then the maximum lift to drag ratio
@@         LDmax = 1/(2·√(CD0·Kind)) and its lift coefficient
@@         CLmd = √(CD0/Kind), tagged.
@@ The points can come from a wind tunnel, or from flight tests
@@ through the Lift and Drag Polar equations of the Equation Library.
@@ Author & design          : Jean Wilson
@@ Co-authors & programming  : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
@@ ============================================================

  → pts
  «
    pts « 1 GET SQ » MAP  pts « 2 GET » MAP  pts SIZE
    → xs ys nn
    «
      IF nn 2 < THEN "PolarFit: at least two points" DOERR END
      xs ΣLIST ys ΣLIST
      0 1 nn FOR ii xs ii GET SQ + NEXT
      0 1 nn FOR ii xs ii GET ys ii GET * + NEXT
      → sx sy sxx sxy
      «
        nn sxx * sx SQ -
        IF DUP 0 == THEN
          "PolarFit: the lift coefficients must differ" DOERR
        END
        nn sxy * sx sy * - SWAP /
        → kf
        «
          sy kf sx * - nn /
          → c0
          «
            c0 "CD0" →TAG
            kf "Kind" →TAG
            1 2 c0 kf * √ * / "LDmax" →TAG
            c0 kf / √ "CLmd" →TAG
          »
        »
      »
    »
  »
»
